events.description:
Come join us for the Opening Reception of "On Self-Respect", a group art exhibition curated by 11.2 featuring the work of Maham Akhtar, Nibha Akireddy, Sharon Li, Nikita Shah, Wei Yuan Wang, and Studio CareFree. 

This exhibition is inspired by Joan Didion’s essay On Self Respect. 11.2 asked artists to interpret the essay however they wanted and the result is a mix of work around identity, self-perception, memory, the body, and what it means to know yourself.

Artists:
@mahkhtar
@nibhaakireddy
@sharonli.studio 
@nikita.untitle
@weiyuan0525
@studiocarefree

Cafe and Wine/Beer menu from Land to Sea will be availble for purchase during this event.  

Limited seating. Open to the public. RSVP is encouraged but not required to attend.

About Us:
11.2 is a curatorial platform exploring art, history, and storytelling run by childhood friends Jen Louie and Ravina Jain. Their goal is to share artists’ stories publicly in ways that feel accessible while honoring the complexity of each artist’s practice. Together, they create projects around stories and perspectives that deserve more attention. 

Land to Sea is a cafe and creative venue committed to curating experiences that inspire creativity, connect people, and fuel the arts & culture of New York City
